<title>LEBANON: Lebanon's SOLIDERE shares rise.</title>
<headline>Lebanon's SOLIDERE shares rise.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Lebanon's biggest company SOLIDERE rose on Wednesday on the privately-operated Beirut Secondary Market (BSM).</p>
<p>A shares rose to $105.5 from Tuesday's $105.0 and B shares rose to $108 from $107.5.</p>
<p>On the Beirut Stock Exchange, there was no trade in any of the four companies, Ciments Libanais, Ciments Blancs, Eternit and Uniceramic. Some 200 Ciments Libanais shares were traded at $1.31 each on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Turnover on BSM, which trades only SOLIDERE shares, fell to 7,206 shares from 13,729 on Tuesday and value was $767,653 from $1,452,594.</p>
<p>The BLOM Stock Index which covers both markets rose 0.4 percent to 922.94 and the LISPI index rose 0.13 percent to 83.02.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 353078 861723</p>
